, or a time is wrong? Tell Fleet: they fix it, say why, and the change is written in a log.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-hours-and-pay-pay-details" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pay details</h2><p class="gd-p">Before your first pay, <b class="gd-ui">My pay</b> asks for your pay details: your full legal name, email, phone, SIN and a photo of a void cheque. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save my pay details</b>. Your SIN is kept encrypted: only Finance and Admin can see it, every look is recorded, and you see only its last 3 digits. How you are paid (bank, e-Transfer) is just below.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-hours-and-pay-your-pay-and-your-pay-statements" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your pay and your pay statements</h2><p class="gd-p">A pay period is two weeks, Sunday to Saturday. An Admin runs the pay after it ends.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The pay is your hours times your hourly rate, plus the commissions and referral fees an Admin approved by the end of the period (see Commissions). Overtime and vacation pay are added only if CarmaCars has switched them on.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">An Admin approves the pay run, pays you (by e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash) and records it. You get an email with the amount and how you were paid.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under Pay statements on <b class="gd-ui">My pay</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">PDF</b> for the statement of a period: your hours day by day, the amounts, the commissions in it and how it was paid.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A pay statement shows no income tax, CPP or EI. They are not worked out in the portal: for your tax slips, ask CarmaCars or your accountant.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-hours-and-pay-where-you-clock-in-and-out" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Where you clock in and out</h2><p class="gd-p">The phone asks for your location once when you clock in and once when you clock out, and never in between. Allow it. If it is off, or you are more than 500 m from the lot, you can still clock in or out: write why in the box that appears, and Fleet sees it.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'report-rentals-referrals-and-profile', 'chapter', 'academy', 'Report anything that happens on the road, add a rental for a renter you found, share your referral link, and keep your details up to date.

## Report a problem

1. Open **Report a problem** and choose the Car.
2. Choose What happened: **New damage found**, **Warning light**, **Collision while I was driving**, **Ticket or toll while I was driving**, **Lost property found** or **Something else**.
3. Write the Details: where, when and what you see.
4. Press **Take a photo** for each photo, then **Send the report**.

![](/guides/img/field-03-report-phone-3b903b20.jpg "phone; size: 390 1040; pins: 1 93.6 46.6, 2 93.6 64.9, 3 93.6 89.9")

> Watch out: In a collision, make sure everyone is safe and call 911 if anyone is hurt. Then call CarmaCars at 289-312-5991 before you send the report.

## Add a rental for a renter you found

Your home address must be in your profile first: until it is, the page asks for it.

1. Open **Add a rental**. Choose the car, the dates and the places, then type the renter''s details. A renter already on file is found by their email. Car already out with the renter? Enter the pickup as when it left: it is recorded as on trip.
2. Press **Check the calendar and the price**. To charge another price, type it with the reason: a price far under the rate sheet is flagged for an Admin, not refused.
3. Choose **Send a payment link** or **Charge the saved card when the renter signs**. The renter pays online: you take no payment for it yourself.
4. Under Who found this client, choose **I sourced this client** or **Entered for CarmaCars**, then press **Add the rental**.

## Commissions

1. You earn 10% of the rental charge (before tax, after discounts, less refunds) of each rental you sourced: one you added and marked I sourced this client, or a booking made with your referral link.
2. It is earned when the rental is completed and paid in full, then an Admin approves it and it is paid on your pay date. Your home address must be in your profile: until it is, a commission waits as not earned yet.
3. **My sales** shows each commission: not earned yet, pending approval, approved, paid or reversed. A refund after payment comes off a later commission.

## Referrals and profile

1. **Referrals**: your own referral link. Press **Copy the link**, or let someone scan its QR code. A booking made with it counts as a rental you sourced.
2. **Profile**: **Save my phone**, your home address (**Change my home address**), **Pay details** (how you are paid: only the last 4 digits of an account number are shown again), **Set up two-step sign-in**, **Change my email** (a link goes to the new address and the old one is told), **Change my password** and **Sign out**.

![](/guides/img/field-04-profile-phone-f05000e2.jpg "phone; size: 390 920; pins: 2 92.3 78.3")

## Sign in with your phone number

Quicker on a phone than a password: a 6-digit code by text.

1. On **Profile**, under Sign-in, press **Add and verify my phone number**, enter your mobile number and press **Text me a code**.
2. Type the code from the text (it usually fills itself in) and press **Verify**. Choose **My phone number (a code by text)** under Sign in with.
3. Next time, the sign-in page opens on your phone number: press **Text me a code** and enter the code. Two-step sign-in still asks for your authenticator code.

## Texts or email

On **Profile**, under **Messages**, choose **Email**, **Text** or **Both** for the messages we send you. Texts need the phone you verified above.

## Phone alerts

Get an alert the moment a job is assigned to you or changes, and when you are paid. Open **Profile**, press **Turn on alerts** under **Phone alerts** and allow notifications. On an iPhone, add CarmaCars to the Home Screen first (Safari, **Share**, **Add to Home Screen**) and turn alerts on from there.

## Alerts

The bell at the top opens **Alerts**: your jobs assigned, changed and running late, and urgent alerts passed to you. With phone alerts on (**Alerts** > **Settings**), they reach your phone too, and at 8 am a short brief of your jobs that day. A late job alert has **Mark picked up** (it opens the booking) and **Snooze 30 min**. Quiet hours (9 pm to 8 am unless you change them) hold the ones that are not urgent.

## Your name and password (release 34)
Open Profile. **Save my display name** changes how you are greeted, at once. Your legal name is the one on your signed agreements, so it is not edited freely: press **Request a name change**, write the full name and why, and an Admin approves it. Until then the name on file stays. To change your email, use Change my email under Sign-in; to add or change your phone, use the phone box under Sign-in (we text a code). **Change my password** sends you to the password page.', 'Report, rentals, referrals and profile', 'Report an incident, add a rental, commissions, your referral link and your profile.',
  'Report anything that happens on the road, add a rental for a renter you found, share your referral link, and keep your details up to date.

## Report a problem

1. On Today, press **Add**, then **A problem with a car**, and choose the Car.
2. Choose What happened: **New damage found**, **Warning light**, **Collision while I was driving**, **Ticket or toll while I was driving**, **Lost property found** or **Something else**.
3. Write the Details: where, when and what you see.
4. Press **Take a photo** for each photo, then **Send the report**.

![](/guides/img/field-03-report-phone-3b903b20.jpg "phone; size: 390 1040; pins: 1 93.6 46.6, 2 93.6 64.9, 3 93.6 89.9")

> Watch out: In a collision, make sure everyone is safe and call 911 if anyone is hurt. Then call CarmaCars at 289-312-5991 before you send the report.

## Add a rental for a renter you found

Your home address must be in your profile first: until it is, the page asks for it.

1. On the Sales tab (or Profile), open **Add a rental**. Choose the car, the dates and the places, then type the renter''s details. A renter already on file is found by their email. Car already out with the renter? Enter the pickup as when it left: it is recorded as on trip.
2. Press **Check the calendar and the price**. To charge another price, type it with the reason: a price far under the rate sheet is flagged for an Admin, not refused.
3. Choose **Send a payment link** or **Charge the saved card when the renter signs**. The renter pays online: you take no payment for it yourself.
4. Under Who found this client, choose **I sourced this client** or **Entered for CarmaCars**, then press **Add the rental**.

## Commissions

1. You earn 10% of the rental charge (before tax, after discounts, less refunds) of each rental you sourced: one you added and marked I sourced this client, or a booking made with your referral link.
2. It is earned when the rental is completed and paid in full, then an Admin approves it and it is paid on your pay date. Your home address must be in your profile: until it is, a commission waits as not earned yet.
3. **My sales** shows each commission: not earned yet, pending approval, approved, paid or reversed. A refund after payment comes off a later commission.

## Do sales too

On **Profile**, press **I want to do sales too**. The Sales path is added to Training; once you pass it, the **Sales** tab opens with the Sales pages. Your field work goes on as before.

## Referrals and profile

1. **Referrals**: your own referral link. Press **Copy the link**, or let someone scan its QR code. A booking made with it counts as a rental you sourced.
2. **Profile**: **Save my phone**, your home address (**Change my home address**), **Pay details** (how you are paid: only the last 4 digits of an account number are shown again), **Set up two-step sign-in**, **Change my email** (a link goes to the new address and the old one is told), **Change my password** and **Sign out**.

![](/guides/img/field-04-profile-phone-f05000e2.jpg "phone; size: 390 920; pins: 2 92.3 78.3")

## Sign in with your phone number

Quicker on a phone than a password: a 6-digit code by text.

1. On **Profile**, under Sign-in, press **Add and verify my phone number**, enter your mobile number and press **Text me a code**.
2. Type the code from the text (it usually fills itself in) and press **Verify**. Choose **My phone number (a code by text)** under Sign in with.
3. Next time, the sign-in page opens on your phone number: press **Text me a code** and enter the code. Two-step sign-in still asks for your authenticator code.

## Texts or email

On **Profile**, under **Messages**, choose **Email**, **Text** or **Both** for the messages we send you. Texts need the phone you verified above.

## Phone alerts

Get an alert the moment a job is assigned to you or changes, and when you are paid. Open **Profile**, press **Turn on alerts** under **Phone alerts** and allow notifications. On an iPhone, add CarmaCars to the Home Screen first (Safari, **Share**, **Add to Home Screen**) and turn alerts on from there.

## Alerts

The bell at the top opens **Alerts**: your jobs assigned, changed and running late, and urgent alerts passed to you. With phone alerts on (**Alerts** > **Settings**), they reach your phone too, and at 8 am a short brief of your jobs that day. A late job alert has **Mark picked up** (it opens the booking) and **Snooze 30 min**. Quiet hours (9 pm to 8 am unless you change them) hold the ones that are not urgent.

## Your name and password (release 34)
Open Profile. **Save my display name** changes how you are greeted, at once. Your legal name is the one on your signed agreements, so it is not edited freely: press **Request a name change**, write the full name and why, and an Admin approves it. Until then the name on file stays. To change your email, use Change my email under Sign-in; to add or change your phone, use the phone box under Sign-in (we text a code). **Change my password** sends you to the password page.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Report anything that happens on the road, add a rental for a renter you found, share your referral link, and keep your details up to date.</p><section class="gd-task" id="report-rentals-referrals-and-profile-report-a-problem" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Report a problem</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--side"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On Today, press <b class="gd-ui">Add</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">A problem with a car</b>, and choose the Car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose What happened: <b class="gd-ui">New damage found</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Warning light</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Collision while I was driving</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Ticket or toll while I was driving</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Lost property found</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Something else</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Write the Details: where, when and what you see.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take a photo</b> for each photo, then <b class="gd-ui">Send the report</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/1040"><img src="/guides/img/field-03-report-phone-3b903b20.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="1040"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:93.6%;top:46.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:93.6%;top:64.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:93.6%;top:89.9%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>In a collision, make sure everyone is safe and call 911 if anyone is hurt. Then call CarmaCars at 289-312-5991 before you send the report.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="report-rentals-referrals-and-profile-add-a-rental-for-a-renter-you-found" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add a rental for a renter you found</h2><p class="gd-p">Your home address must be in your profile first: until it is, the page asks for it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the Sales tab (or Profile), open <b class="gd-ui">Add a rental</b>. Choose the car, the dates and the places, then type the renter&#39;s details. A renter already on file is found by their email. Car already out with the renter? Enter the pickup as when it left: it is recorded as on trip.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Check the calendar and the price</b>. To charge another price, type it with the reason: a price far under the rate sheet is flagged for an Admin, not refused.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Choose <b class="gd-ui">Send a payment link</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Charge the saved card when the renter signs</b>. The renter pays online: you take no payment for it yourself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Under Who found this client, choose <b class="gd-ui">I sourced this client</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Entered for CarmaCars</b>, then press <b class="gd-ui">Add the rental</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="report-rentals-referrals-and-profile-commissions" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Commissions</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">You earn 10% of the rental charge (before tax, after discounts, less refunds) of each rental you sourced: one you added and marked I sourced this client, or a booking made with your referral link.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">It is earned when the rental is completed and paid in full, then an Admin approves it and it is paid on your pay date. Your home address must be in your profile: until it is, a commission waits as not earned yet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">My sales</b> shows each commission: not earned yet, pending approval, approved, paid or reversed. A refund after payment comes off a later commission.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="report-rentals-referrals-and-profile-do-sales-too" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Do sales too</h2><p class="gd-p">On <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">I want to do sales too</b>. The Sales path is added to Training; once you pass it, the <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b> tab opens with the Sales pages. Your field work goes on as before.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="report-rentals-referrals-and-profile-referrals-and-profile" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Referrals and profile</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--side"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Referrals</b>: your own referral link. Press <b class="gd-ui">Copy the link</b>, or let someone scan its QR code. A booking made with it counts as a rental you sourced.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Save my phone</b>, your home address (<b class="gd-ui">Change my home address</b>), <b class="gd-ui">Pay details</b> (how you are paid: only the last 4 digits of an account number are shown again), <b class="gd-ui">Set up two-step sign-in</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Change my email</b> (a link goes to the new address and the old one is told), <b class="gd-ui">Change my password</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Sign out</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/920"><img src="/guides/img/field-04-profile-phone-f05000e2.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="920"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:92.3%;top:78.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="report-rentals-referrals-and-profile-sign-in-with-your-phone-number" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sign in with your phone number</h2><p class="gd-p">Quicker on a phone than a password: a 6-digit code by text.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>, under Sign-in, press <b class="gd-ui">Add and verify my phone number</b>, enter your mobile number and press <b class="gd-ui">Text me a code</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Type the code from the text (it usually fills itself in) and press <b class="gd-ui">Verify</b>. Choose <b class="gd-ui">My phone number (a code by text)</b> under Sign in with.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Next time, the sign-in page opens on your phone number: press <b class="gd-ui">Text me a code</b> and enter the code. Two-step sign-in still asks for your authenticator code.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="report-rentals-referrals-and-profile-texts-or-email" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Texts or email</h2><p class="gd-p">On <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>, under <b class="gd-ui">Messages</b>, choose <b class="gd-ui">Email</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Both</b> for the messages we send you. Texts need the phone you verified above.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="report-rentals-referrals-and-profile-phone-alerts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Phone alerts</h2><p class="gd-p">Get an alert the moment a job is assigned to you or changes, and when you are paid. Open <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">Turn on alerts</b> under <b class="gd-ui">Phone alerts</b> and allow notifications. On an iPhone, add CarmaCars to the Home Screen first (Safari, <b class="gd-ui">Share</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Add to Home Screen</b>) and turn alerts on from there.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="report-rentals-referrals-and-profile-alerts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Alerts</h2><p class="gd-p">The bell at the top opens <b class="gd-ui">Alerts</b>: your jobs assigned, changed and running late, and urgent alerts passed to you. With phone alerts on (<b class="gd-ui">Alerts</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>), they reach your phone too, and at 8 am a short brief of your jobs that day. A late job alert has <b class="gd-ui">Mark picked up</b> (it opens the booking) and <b class="gd-ui">Snooze 30 min</b>. Quiet hours (9 pm to 8 am unless you change them) hold the ones that are not urgent.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="report-rentals-referrals-and-profile-your-name-and-password-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your name and password (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">Open Profile. <b class="gd-ui">Save my display name</b> changes how you are greeted, at once. Your legal name is the one on your signed agreements, so it is not edited freely: press <b class="gd-ui">Request a name change</b>, write the full name and why, and an Admin approves it. Until then the name on file stays. To change your email, use Change my email under Sign-in; to add or change your phone, use the phone box under Sign-in (we text a code). <b class="gd-ui">Change my password</b> sends you to the password page.</p></section>');
